{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAttestation staleness errors currently say the plan changed in the fixed list \"description/AC/file_impact/children\". That is misleading: AC is not an independent material key, checkbox state is normalized out, and the message does not identify the component that actually changed. Operator approval: fix this broadly anywhere rebar reports an attestation refusal, including additive signed-manifest metadata, while preserving all gate outcomes.\n\n## Confirmed RCA\n\n`material_fingerprint()` hashes a single composite basis. Current `origin/main` keeps the basis single-sourced in `material_diff.material_basis`: `ticket_id`, normalized `description`, `file_impact`, `children`, and conditional `file_impact_scope`; `pass1.material_fingerprint()` hashes that basis. Checkbox state is removed by `normalize_checkbox_state()`, so ticking `- [ ]` to `- [x]` is attestation-safe. Because the composite hash is one-way and older manifests lack per-component values, stale-material readers could not name what changed and sometimes named the fictional `AC` component.\n\n## Plan\n\nAdd/keep signed per-component material fingerprints as deterministic additive `material-part: <name> <hash16> <size>` manifest lines. Parse them leniently and use them only for diagnostics. On stale-material, compare signed parts with live parts and render the changed component(s) plus compact sizes; legacy manifests fall back to child-pin add/remove diffs when possible, otherwise say the component cannot be named and advise re-review. Update every attestation-refusal surface that drops or rewrites the underlying reason so it forwards or reconstructs the same specific reason.\n\nInvariant: no gate outcome changes. Edits may only add manifest diagnostic lines or change `reason` text for already-failing branches. Do not change branch conditions, verdict names, thresholds, or valid/invalid decisions.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py`: per-component material hashing and explanation.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py`: emit/parse additive `material-part:` lines.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py`: named stale-material reasons and timestamped stale-reopened reasons.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py`: actionable unsigned message and complete verdict docs.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/generation.py`: named own/dependency material drift.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py`: named plan drift in sign-review recovery.\n- `src/rebar/llm/completion_child_gate.py`: forward child closure signature reason.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py`: sign-aborted rendering that names reason/remedy.\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md`: document checkbox-safe and named staleness reasons.\n- `tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py`: regression coverage.\n\n## Testing / Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `material_components(ctx)` exposes exactly the material basis keys and changing one component changes only that component hash.\n- [ ] `build_manifest` emits sorted `material-part` lines and `manifest_material_parts()` round-trips them; manifests without lines parse to `{}`.\n- [ ] `compute_validity` stale-material reasons name changed components for description-only, file-impact-only, and children-only edits, never `description/AC/file_impact/children`.\n- [ ] Tick-only checkbox edits remain `verdict == \"certified\"`.\n- [ ] Legacy raw-description attestations over unchanged tickets remain certified; un-grandfatherable legacy attestations say the changed component cannot be named.\n- [ ] `stale-reopened` names signed/reopened timestamps; `unsigned` names both `review-plan` and `sign-review` remedies.\n- [ ] `plan_review_sign_aborted` with `store-read-failure` renders that reason and does not advise `sign-review`.\n- [ ] Generation-time dependency material drift names changed dependency ticket ids.\n- [ ] Touched branches preserve the prior `(valid, verdict)` outcome; relevant unit/integration tests pass.\n- [ ] Documentation states plainly that ticking an AC checkbox is attestation-safe.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788233599999902001,"uuid":"87ca8ea1-7eb6-4adc-96c7-c48c60249911"}